### create a public room to invite into (run first, then replace :id below with the returned id) -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/new HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "respond flow room",
	"visibility": "public"
}

### owner (user 1) invites user 6 -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{}

### invitee (user 6) accepts -> 200, status becomes "accepted"
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### invitee accepts again while already accepted -> 200, idempotent no-op (returns as-is, no re-processing)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### re-inviting user 6 after they already accepted -> 201, status stays "accepted"
### regression check: resolveInvitation() must NOT reset an accepted invitation back to
### "pending" just because someone sends another invite (see invitation.service.ts)
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{}

### create a second room to test the decline path (run first, then replace :id2 below with the returned id) -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/new HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"name": "decline flow room",
	"visibility": "public"
}

### owner invites user 6 into the second room -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{}

### invitee (user 6) declines -> 200, status becomes "rejected"
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "rejected"
}

### re-inviting user 6 after they declined -> 201, status resets to "pending" (a fresh invite is allowed)
POST http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{}

### inviter (user 1) tries to respond to the invitation they sent -> 403 Forbidden (only the invitee can respond)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 1

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### unrelated third party (user 3) tries to respond -> 403 Forbidden
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 3

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### trying to set status back to "pending" -> 400 Bad Request (zod excludes "pending" from the update schema)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "pending"
}

### invalid status value -> 400 Bad Request (zod enum mismatch)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "maybe"
}

### responding to an invitation that doesn't exist for this room/user pair -> 404 Not Found
### (user 3 was never invited to this room)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/3 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 3

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### missing x-user-id header -> 401 Unauthorized
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### x-user-id with no matching user in DB -> 401 Unauthorized
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/:id2/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 999999

{
	"status": "accepted"
}

### non-integer room id -> 400 Bad Request (ParseIntPipe)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/rooms/abc/invitations/6 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: 6

{
	"status": "accepted"
}
